{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act pre-offer criminal record inquiry ban","requirement":"A housing provider may not require an applicant to complete a housing application asking about criminal record, or make any oral or written inquiry about it, before issuing a conditional offer.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; pre-offer inquiry allowed into methamphetamine production convictions on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex offender registration.","penalty":"Director may impose monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations, and order remedies including a conditional offer or unit.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include review of criminal history and that the applicant may provide evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation, or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require the applicant’s rental application fee to be returned and may impose monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act limits on criminal record consideration","requirement":"A housing provider may not evaluate an applicant on arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated, sealed, or juvenile records, and after a conditional offer may consider only specified convictions within set lookback periods.","key_value":"6-year / 4-year / 1-year lookback by offense degree after conditional offer","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may impose monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations, and order remedial action.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-56","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not, either before or after the issuance of a conditional offer, evaluate an applicant based on any of the following types of criminal records: (1) arrests or charges that have not resulted in a criminal conviction;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act advertising restriction","requirement":"A housing provider may not knowingly or purposefully publish a housing advertisement stating that it will not consider any applicant who has been arrested or convicted of one or more crimes or offenses, subject to limited exceptions.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; advertisements about methamphetamine production convictions on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex offender registration.","penalty":"Director may impose monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations, and order remedial action.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-58","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not knowingly or purposefully publish, or cause to be published, any housing advertisement that explicitly provides that the housing provider will not consider any applicant who has been arrested or convicted of one or more crimes or offenses","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act drug and alcohol test ban","requirement":"A housing provider may not require an applicant to submit to a drug or alcohol test, or request the applicant’s consent to obtain information from a drug abuse treatment facility.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may impose monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations, and order remedial action.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-60","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to submit to a drug or alcohol test, or request the applicant’s consent to obtain information from a drug abuse treatment facility.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction of former applicant after successful appeal of Fair Chance order","requirement":"If a housing provider’s appeal succeeds and the court overturns the director’s order, the provider may evict the former applicant housed under that order so long as it gives at least 45 days’ notice before the eviction.","key_value":"at least 45 days’ notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of a director’s order under this act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Applies to a former applicant housed under a director’s order"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Operates notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
